      "content": "the distinction on power vs latency is a good angle. but i'm looking closer at that 2018 patent (10,456,789). it seems to mention similar asynchronous mechanisms for reducing latency during task distribution, not just power. \n\nbefore i finalize this, can you double check the 2018 patent against the DNPU specs? i want to be 100% sure there isn't any overlap in the actual scheduling logic that an examiner might use to reject our novelty claim. if there's any risk, i need to know now.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
